# 7. If Jenkins still says "Failed to connect"

Go to:

**Manage Jenkins → Nodes → aws-agent → Log**

The error will normally tell us which one it is:

```text
Permission denied (publickey)
```

→ Wrong private key / username.

```text
Connection timed out
```

→ AWS Security Group doesn't allow TCP 22.

```text
Host key verification failed
```

→ Host-key configuration issue.

```text
java: command not found
```

→ Java isn't installed on AWS.

```text
Agent is connected
```

→ SSH setup is working.

### Most important test

Before changing anything else in Jenkins, run this **from the GCP Jenkins controller**:

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/kp-1.pem ubuntu@<AWS_PUBLIC_IP>
```

**If this does not successfully log into AWS, the Jenkins credential will not work either.**

